lisa-design:
- One read-only credential per private read repo ({contents: read}), so each token fits one App installation and the agent maps repo→token directly; lists omitted when empty; refreshed with the task token.
- Task (rw) token covers only its repo; GitCredentialRequest.Validate refuses ReadRepos on any token that can write.
- Private vs public decided by the TaskSpec (workspace.publicReads → credentials.git.publicReads at compile time): true = read repos cloned anonymously, no token; else every read repo gets a read token. Limitation documented: can't mix private repos with public repos outside the App's installations.
- Mint is all-or-nothing; a failed read mint leaves the task Pending (git-credential); tokens never stored, credentialExpiresAt = earliest expiry.
